  {
    "insert": "\nThis exposé aims to investigate how AI can benefit both students and teachers in improving mathematical skills. The approach builds on established frameworks such as Davis’ Technology Acceptance Model and Piaget’s constructivist learning theory. The proposed methodology includes interviews and feedback loops with teachers and students, followed by a pilot test of a personalized AI learning platform. Juji and Microsoft Azure OpenAI are evaluated as possible implementation platforms, each offering distinct advantages in usability and customization.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Strength",
    "attributes": {
      "size": "large"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\nThe author uses established frameworks (Davis' Technology Acceptance Model and Piaget’s learning theory) to justify design and research direction. Theoretical relevance is well demonstrated and directly linked to the central research question."
  },
